From deed314a45fa093b53e6f2008e11a70456ec8831 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Frdlik <michaelf.ms@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 13:35:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Thylacine Warp multi-queue (F3): per-timeline fences +
 transport mutex + witnesses

The multi-queue submit-fence redesign, client half (WARP-MULTIQUEUE-DESIGN in
the Thylacine tree; ratified fence-ABI v2 -- the timelines file + the shared
park):

- warp_client: warp_venus_submit carries the venus TIMELINE and is NON-PARKING
  (the fence file admits ONE parked reader -- the server keeps a single
  per-ctx report cursor -- so a throttle park inside a mutex-holding submit
  would deadlock against the renderer's parker; a full throttle/lane reports
  *again instead). The timeline rides the FILE (submit1..3; submit = timeline
  0) because the payload is opaque bytes and t_write's implicit offset rules
  out offset-encoding. Per-timeline t_issued/t_signaled ledgers + the
  timelines-file refresh (warp_timelines_refresh) + the bare park primitive
  (warp_fence_park: one blocking read, no state mutation -- the caller does
  all bookkeeping under its own mutex).

- vn_renderer_thylacine: the transport mutex lands (the owed F6/F8
  per-renderer mutex, now a dependency of concurrent multi-queue submits) +
  the one-parker/condvar protocol (the mutex is NEVER held across the park).
  thylacine_submit threads batch->ring_idx end-to-end with a bounded
  non-parking retry loop; syncs bind (timeline, seq); thylacine_wait waits
  per-timeline through the parker. max_timeline_count lifts to 4 (3 VkQueues
  + the CPU lane, the ratified v1.0 bound) gated on the host capset's
  supports_multiple_timelines (degenerate hosts keep 2); the forced
  supports_multiple_timelines=0 is dropped -- the seam now carries timelines.

- thylacine_prove: four new witnesses, all green on thyla-pi/KVM real V3D
  4.2.14: the F1 reify-at-alloc fix-proof (vkCmdCopyBuffer + fenced
  vkQueueSubmit + vkWaitForFences + FIRST-map pattern survival -- the first
  GPU round-trip executed on Thylacine), the F4 placed-map de-advertisement
  check (76 device exts scanned), the timeline lift (a second logical device
  acquires ring_idx 2 -- refused under the old count of 2), and the F2
  cap-exhaustion recovery cycle (refusal at the 64 MiB ctx cap burns no
  handle state). Queue getter goes direct to vk_common_GetDeviceQueue2 and
  buffers use the `2` forms -- the link is the census: the flat forms are not
  defined symbols in libvulkan_virtio.a.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
